{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"848d4a9e465c042cff882139271764a09b08a5e6369fb8955be7c60fdbe11177","packTokens":1782,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":252,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":383,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1041,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"A web front end with a small API and a database behind it.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"The app ships with exactly 8 requests.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Requests are stored in the database and survive a reload and a restart.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"The API needs these four operations and no others: list, create, get by ID, and change status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Requests screen with status filters, create dialog, and loading, empty, and error states.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Request detail screen with status-appropriate action, update failure state, and not-found state.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Clean light theme, responsive layout, accessible controls, and specified badge colors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Automated tests for the business rules and one end-to-end workflow.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"If the user creates a request while a status filter other than All is selected, how should the list behave after successful creation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Switch the filter to All so the new Open request appears at the top.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which browsers must the web app support?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No specific browser support target beyond browsers compatible with the chosen implementation.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If the create API call fails for a reason other than field validation, what should the dialog show?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Show “Could not create request.” in the dialog, keep the entered values, and allow retry.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How should surrounding whitespace in a title affect requiredness, length validation, and the stored title?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Trim surrounding whitespace before validating and storing the title.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"After a successful status change on the detail screen, what should happen to the Requests list when the user returns to it?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the selected filter and refresh the list; the request may disappear if it no longer matches the filter.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build a maintenance request system with a browser-accessible Requests interface, an HTTP API, and a database that persists request records across reloads and restarts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"On first initialization of an empty database, seed exactly eight requests: four Open (exactly one Urgent), two In progress, and two Done, with every supported area represented.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Expose exactly four API operations: list requests, create a request, get a request by ID, and change its status; reject API edits to fixed fields and deletion.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"List all requests or those matching one status, ordered newest first. On creation, assign a generated ID, UTC creation time, and Open status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Validate trimmed titles of 3–80 characters, areas of Kitchen, Meeting room, Open desk, Washroom, or Reception, priorities of Low, Normal, or Urgent, and optional descriptions no longer than 500 characters; reject invalid values with an error naming the field.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Allow only the status transitions Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open; reject all other status changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Show the Hive Works wordmark, demo-user initials SC, status filters All/Open/In progress/Done with All initially selected, a New request button, and a newest-first request list on the Requests screen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Refresh the list when a status filter is selected or the user returns from detail, retain the selected filter on return, and after successful creation close the dialog, select All, and show the new request at the top.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"The New request dialog shall have labeled Title, Area, Priority, and Description fields, Normal as the default priority, and Create and Cancel controls; show field validation errors under their fields, and on other creation failures show “Could not create request.”, retain entered values, and allow retry.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Show “Loading requests…” while loading, “No requests here.” when the selected filter has no matches, and “Could not load requests.” with a Retry button when loading fails.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Show request detail with a back link, title, area, priority and status badges, created date, and description or “No description.”; show Start work for Open, Mark done for In progress, and Reopen for Done.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"After a successful status change, show the new status and corresponding action; after failure, show “Could not update the request.” and retain the prior status. For an unknown ID, show “Request not found.” and a link back to Requests, and have the API identify the request as not found.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Use a light theme, sans-serif font, neutral background, near-black text, and labeled badges with Open blue, In progress amber, Done green, Urgent red, and Low and Normal neutral.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Display created dates as date-only values such as “8 Oct 2026,” without time or timezone. Use stacked request cards at 375 px and table rows at 1280 px, avoid horizontal page scrolling at those widths, label every field, make every control keyboard reachable, and meet WCAG AA text contrast.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Include automated business-rule tests for the specified creation validation, allowed and disallowed transitions, filtered newest-first listing, and unknown-ID behavior, plus an end-to-end list-to-completion workflow that verifies the created request appears at the top and then in the Done-filtered list.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}